## Key findings
1. Restaurant competition: spending gap between dining out and grocery shopping exceeded $20 billion as of December 2024.
2. Grocery-anchored retail strength: vacancy compressed to 3.5% in Q4 2024, down 10 basis points from Q4 2023 and 100 basis points below the 4.5% pandemic peak in Q2 2021.
3. Investment performance: multi-tenant grocery-anchored retail transactions totaled $7.0 billion in 2024, up 1.4% from 2023; average price per square foot reached a record high of $209.
4. Aldi expansion: added 105 new locations in 2024, totaling over 2.3 million square feet.
5. M&A activity: FTC blocked the Kroger-Albertsons merger; Aldi acquired Southeastern Grocers (220 Winn-Dixie and Harvey Supermarkets); Grocery Outlet acquired United Grocery Outlet (40-store chain).
6. Private label growth: private-label brand sales reached over $270 billion in 2024, up 3.4% from 2023; market share rose to 20.7% in 2024, up 160 basis points from 2021.
7. SNAP integration: over 41.7 million SNAP participants (12% of U.S. population) gained access to on-demand grocery delivery through platform integrations by Instacart, GoPuff, Uber Eats, Shipt, and Thrive Market.
8. Retail media networks: ad spending reached nearly $52 billion in 2024, up 20.4% from 2023; forecasted to reach nearly $100 billion by 2028.

## State of the grocery industry

Dining vs. grocery spending:
- Gap widened from $3.4 billion in January 2022 to over $21 billion by end of 2024.
- Dining out spending rose 4.4% in 2024 vs. 2023; grocery spending increased 1.8%.
- Pandemic prompted a shift from goods to services as consumers sought social experiences.

Foot traffic trends:
- Grocery industry foot traffic declined 11.4% in 2020, bounced back to pre-pandemic levels in 2022 (up 5.9% from 2019).
- Reached 17.2 billion visits in 2024, up 1.0% from 2023 and 10.9% from 2019.
- Average in-store dwell time: 23.4 minutes in 2024, down 0.3 minutes from 2023 and 1.4 minutes from 2019.

Discount & specialty grocers:
- Aldi foot traffic: 900+ million visits in 2024, up 51.2% from 2019 (vs. 600 million average 2019-2021).
- Grocery Outlet foot traffic: nearly 130 million visits in 2024, up 48.7% from 2019 (vs. 87 million average 2019-2021).
- Trader Joe's foot traffic: nearly 390 million in 2024, up 6.1% from 2023 and 24.7% from 2019.

Market concentration: top 10 grocers accounted for nearly 44% of total industry visit share in 2024.

## Grocery-anchored retail fundamentals

Vacancy & supply:
- Q4 2024 vacancy: 3.5%.
- Net absorption 2024: nearly 300,000 sq. ft. (down 37.9% from 2023).
- Net deliveries: under 100,000 sq. ft. for a second consecutive year (vs. 2.1 million sq. ft. average 2015-2019 for absorption; 1.1 million for deliveries).
- Available space decreased 7.5 million sq. ft. from the Q1 2021 pandemic high.
- Lost nearly 19 million sq. ft. (50%) since the post-Great Recession high.

Rent growth:
- Grocery-anchored retail: 3.1% annual rent growth in Q4 2024 (highest among retail subtypes).
- Neighborhood centers: 2.9% annual rent growth.
- Power centers: 2.9% annual rent growth.

## Investment activity

2024 transaction data:
- Multi-tenant grocery transactions: $7.0 billion (1.4% increase from 2023).
- Second half 2024: transaction volume rose 34%.
- Average price per sq. ft.: record high of $209 in 2024.

Investor composition shift (2024 vs. 2023):
- Private capital: decreased from 74% to 68%.
- REITs increasingly active: Brixmor, Phillips Edison & Co, Cohen & Steers, ShopOne, Agree Realty, Regency Centers.
- Operators/grocers reached an eight-year high in investment levels; key players include Publix, Trader Joe's, Walmart, H Mart, Weis Markets.

## Fastest-growing grocers 2024

National expansion leaders:
- Aldi: 105 new locations, 2.3 million sq. ft. added.
- Publix: 43 new locations, 2 million sq. ft. (over 50% in Florida).
- H-E-B: 9 new locations, 1 million sq. ft. (Texas).
- Sprouts: 35 new stores, just under 840,000 sq. ft.
- Trader Joe's: 34 new locations, over 450,000 sq. ft.
- Fresh Market: 8 new locations, just under 200,000 sq. ft.
- Amazon Fresh: 21 new locations, under 900,000 sq. ft.

Future growth plans:
- Aldi announced 225+ new store openings planned for 2025 (doubling previous years); five-year plan targets 800 new stores by 2028.
- Grocery Outlet: expanding Southeast through United Grocery Outlet acquisition; entering Delaware and strengthening Mid-Atlantic presence.
- Sprouts: entering Wyoming; increasing presence in Delaware, South Carolina, Virginia (new store openings up 16.7% in 2024).
- Publix: entered eighth Southeastern state (Kentucky) in early 2024.
- H-E-B: continuing Texas focus.

Canadian grocers: Loblaw growing Maxi in Quebec and No Frills elsewhere; Empire expanding FreshCo in Western Canada; Metro opening a dozen new locations, mostly discount stores including Super C and Food Basics.

