## Private label brands

Sales & market share:
- 2024 private-label sales: over $270 billion (up 3.4% from 2023).
- Four-year growth: $51.7 billion increase (23.6%).
- Market share: 20.7% in 2024 (up 160 basis points from 2021).

Major grocer programs:
- Kroger Our Brands: over $31 billion of $150 billion total sales (FY 2023).
- Albertsons Our Brands: over $16.5 billion of $79.2 billion total sales (FY 2023).

New private label launches 2024: Sprouts Real Root (personal care, October); Albertsons Bee Lightly (wine, September) and Overjoyed (treats, September); Amazon Saver (under $5 essentials with 10% Prime discount, September); Grocery Outlet Go Brands (SimplyGo, Home & Haven, Paw & Pamper, September); Kroger Field & Vine (produce, July); Giant Food New Coast Foraging Company (grocery basics, February); SpartanNash Finest Reserve (pizzas, pastas, spices, wine, February).

## Inflation & pricing
- "Food at home" inflation remained below 2% throughout 2024 (peaked mid-2022).
- "Food away from home" inflation: 3.6% in December 2024 (70 basis points above overall inflation of 2.9%; 190 basis points above food-at-home at 1.8%).
- Cost elevation since February 2020: "food at home" up 26.8%; "food away from home" up 29.3%.

## SNAP & grocery accessibility
- FY 2024: over 41 million participants (12% of U.S. population); up 16.8% from FY 2019.
- Average monthly benefit FY 2024: $187 (up 44.3% from FY 2019).
- FY 2013 peak: 47.6 million participants (15% of population); average benefit $133.
- Third-party SNAP integration in 2024: Instacart (Nov., eligibility screener), GoPuff (Nov., first instant-commerce retailer with USDA approval), Uber Eats (Oct., nationwide SNAP acceptance at select Albertsons grocers), Shipt (June, Target/Meijer deliveries), Thrive Market (Feb., first online-only retailer with USDA approval).

## Grocery e-commerce
- 2024 forecast: nearly $204 billion (10.7% increase from 2023).
- Four-year projection: $270+ billion by end of 2028 (7.4% CAGR).
- Notable delivery-platform partnerships expanded throughout 2024 (DoorDash, Instacart, Uber Eats, Shipt, Grubhub, Amazon) across numerous regional and national grocers.

## Retail media networks
- 2024 ad spending: nearly $52 billion (20.4% increase from 2023).
- 2028 forecast: nearly $100 billion (17.1% CAGR; projected doubling).
- National and regional grocers (Albertsons, Kroger, Hy-Vee, Save A Lot, Ahold Delhaize, ShopRite, and others) expanded retail media / in-store digital advertising partnerships throughout 2024.

## Future considerations

For grocery-anchored retail:
- Demand-supply mismatch expected to persist; minimal new supply anticipated.
- Record-low vacancy and availabilities expected to continue.
- Landlords positioned for continued rent growth.
- Investor interest projected to remain strong due to stable returns and tenant stability.

For the grocery industry:
- Elevated costs will sustain demand for discount grocers and private-label expansion.
- Grocers will enhance retail media networks to compete with restaurants as the goods-to-services shift intensifies.
- E-commerce growth will continue as consumers seek deals and SNAP access expands.
- Over 12% of the U.S. population expected to remain SNAP-eligible short-term.

